  "_source": "Hand-verified directly against RCA-DFC-REG-002.md's real per-field bit tables (0x2300-0x236C), cited by contract ID below -- same disclosed scope/rationale as every prior field-map file's own _source note (extract_registers.py does not currently preserve per-field bit ranges project-wide). RTL010_EVT_OVERFLOW_STATUS's status_registers entry below (EVENT_OVERFLOW/DROP_COUNT mapped to the generic status_o.event_overflow/event_drop_count fields dfc_rtl010_status_t carries) closes the readback gap from the start, same discipline rtl006/007/008/009_field_map.json established (OPEN_ISSUES.md item 21). SENSOR0_STATUS/SENSOR1_STATUS/SENSOR_STATUS each appear in BOTH control_registers (their real W1C clear-request fields) AND status_registers (their real RO/W1C-readback fields) -- same dual-appearance pattern already used for RTL-007/008/009's own per-channel STATUS registers. dfc_rtl010_control_t grew 345->346 bits this session (approved before implementation) to add rtl010_evt_overflow_status__event_overflow at the new highest bit (345), closing the ninth real instance of the EVENT_OVERFLOW-clear-field gap class (items 2/7/8/12/20/24/28/32). SENSOR_UPDATE_SELECT/SENSOR_UPDATE_VALUE/SENSOR_UPDATE_META are plain internal_reg staging registers (host writes land directly in RTL-001's own storage and are forwarded into control_i every cycle, matching REG-002's own 'staged fields do not alter active state until commit' text) -- no status_registers entry needed since a host read simply returns what RTL-001 itself stored, not an RTL-010 echo. SENSOR_UPDATE_COMMIT is a WO-CMD register (readback=zero in dfc_registers_pkg.json); its COMMIT bit is forwarded as a real one-cycle command pulse via reggen.py's existing WO-CMD pulse-capture mechanism, identical in kind to SENSOR009/007/008's own RTL009_EVT_OVERFLOW_STATUS-class W1C forwarding. SENSOR0_MAX_AGE_MS/SENSOR0_THRESH_LOW/SENSOR0_THRESH_HIGH/SENSOR0_EVENT_IRQ_CFG/SENSOR0_HYSTERESIS (and the SENSOR1 equivalents) are plain internal_reg RW registers: control-only, no status_registers entry (a host read returns RTL-001's own stored value, not an RTL-010 echo, same pattern as every other module's plain configuration RW register e.g. PULSE0_THRESH_LOW_Q17_15). Confirmed directly against dfc_registers_pkg.json: SENSOR_STATUS/SENSOR0_VALUE/SENSOR0_STATUS/SENSOR0_CURRENT_AGE_MS/SENSOR1_VALUE/SENSOR1_STATUS/SENSOR1_CURRENT_AGE_MS/RTL010_EVT_OVERFLOW_STATUS/SENSOR0_META/SENSOR1_META are all readback=external; SENSOR_CONTROL/SENSOR_UPDATE_SELECT/SENSOR_UPDATE_VALUE/SENSOR_UPDATE_META/SENSOR0_MAX_AGE_MS/SENSOR0_THRESH_LOW/SENSOR0_THRESH_HIGH/SENSOR0_EVENT_IRQ_CFG/SENSOR1_MAX_AGE_MS/SENSOR1_THRESH_LOW/SENSOR1_THRESH_HIGH/SENSOR1_EVENT_IRQ_CFG/SENSOR0_HYSTERESIS/SENSOR1_HYSTERESIS are all readback=internal_reg; SENSOR_UPDATE_COMMIT is readback=zero.",
